    "cons": [
      "Costs noticeably more than other 120V MIG welders",
      "3/16-inch mild steel maximum, per Miller",
      "Aluminum requires a separate spool gun"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "If you weld for longer stretches on 120V and want the machine to set itself up, the Millermatic 142's duty cycle and Auto-Set justify its premium."
  },
  {
    "id": "hobart-handler-210-mvp",
    "name": "Hobart Handler 210 MVP MIG Welder",
    "badge": "Best Dual-Voltage",
    "category": "115V / 230V MIG / Flux-Core",
