    "description": "The Handler 210 MVP is for the beginner who already knows they will outgrow 120 volts, usually because trailers, farm equipment or thick brackets are on the list. Hobart's specification lists 25 to 140 amps on 115 volts and 25 to 210 amps on 230 volts, with rated outputs of 90 amps at 20 percent duty cycle on 115 volts and 150 amps at 30 percent on 230 volts. Its single-pass mild steel range is listed as 24 gauge to 3/8 inch, though that top figure needs 230-volt power; one retailer-side source suggests 1/4 inch is the practical limit on 115 volts. The MVP plug system lets you swap between household and 230-volt receptacles without tools. It is heavier and pricier than a 120-volt-only machine, and you only get its real advantage if you have, or will install, a 230-volt circuit.",
    "pros": [
      "Switches between 115V and 230V without tools, per Hobart",
      "Up to 210 amps on 230V",
      "Rated to 3/8-inch mild steel on 230V",
      "Room to grow from sheet metal to heavier plate",
      "Spool gun ready for aluminum"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Needs a 230V circuit to reach its full rating",
      "Heavier and more expensive than 120V-only machines",
      "Duty cycle at 230V is a modest 30 percent at 150A"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "Buy the Handler 210 MVP if thicker steel is in your future and you have, or will add, a 230V outlet; on 115V alone, a 140-class welder is enough."
  },
  {
    "id": "lincoln-easy-mig-140",
    "name": "Lincoln Electric Easy-MIG 140 (K2697-1)",
